  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "The length of a rectangle is twice its width. The perimeter is 13 cm. Let $x$ cm be the width. Write an equation for $x$ and find the width and length.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$6x=13$; width $2\\frac{1}{6}$ cm, length $4\\frac{1}{3}$ cm.",
      "worked": "The length is $2x$ cm. Using the sum of the four sides:\n$$\\begin{align*}x+2x+x+2x&=13\\\\6x&=13\\\\x&=\\frac{13}{6}\\\\x&=2\\frac{1}{6}\\end{align*}$$\nThe width is $2\\frac{1}{6}$ cm and the length is $2\\times\\frac{13}{6}=\\frac{13}{3}=4\\frac{1}{3}$ cm.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
